{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229520-2e-how-much-space-between-demesne","id":1229520,"title":"2E - How much space between Demesne?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T22:46:03-07:00","id":1229520,"title":"2E - How much space between Demesne?","content":"When you have a Solar standing at the edge of Creation and is ready to create some more land and a Demesne to put on top of it, just how much land does he need to create in between Demesne? Particularly the powerful ones? I seem to remember a passage about Lookshy indicating that they don\u2019t normally exist too close to one another. Does a Solar need to build his Level 5 Demesne about 20 miles apart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T06:29:30-07:00","id":1229578,"title":"","content":"I can't say I have an actual answer, but some ideas...<br /> <br /> There is a passage in one of the books about two Demesnes or Manses pulled closer to each other, which creates a lot of strain. I took that strain to mainly be because the those power sources are moved from their original locations, than because they now are close together.<br /> <br /> Still, I think there should be a minimal distance between two Demesnes (possible being able to place them closer for an extra cost). If they are of different types, they also probably can be closer to each other than two of the same type, because of the available essence flow in the area.<br /> <br /> So by shaping the essence flow from four different directions, it would probably be possible to put four powerful Demesnes fairly close; while making those areas quite void of other Demesnes of the same kind.<br /> <br /> Another problem I have myself with the rule as written is that I think it should be harder to create a Demesne free area than one with a bunch of random ones. So I will probably at some time make my own rewrite where there will be X dices of power per area, and those will lead to a bunch of Demesnes of various kinds with a random areal spread; unless the Solar spends shaping points to control the process.<br /> <br /> The natural spread of level 5 Demesnes is probably at least a couple of hundreds of miles apart, with a bunch of weaker ones in between. By shaping those weaker ones to flow into more powerful nodes, it probably would be possible to place 3-5 level 5 Demesnes within 10 miles of each other, but each using up all essence line powers of a 1000 square miles area or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T10:17:16-07:00","id":1229614,"title":"","content":"And how do you factor in Dragon Blooded who become powerful Demesne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T10:52:36-07:00","id":1229617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229520-2e-how-much-space-between-demesne?p=1229614#post1229614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you factor in Dragon Blooded who become powerful Demesne?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? I didn't knew that was a possibility, and if I ever read that I have forgotten it (most likely from ignoring it).<br /> <br /> In my mind, a Demesne is a bit of a spring, where the ground water breaks the surface. So in that type of comparison, someone becoming a Demesne would be like digging a well; and pumping up a lot of water from a well will usually not bode well for the groundwater in the area in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T11:34:37-07:00","id":1229621,"title":"","content":"It is an Awareness Charm called Earth Reclaims Her Bounty. It transforms a DB into a Demesne of a level equal to her Breeding score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T11:52:46-07:00","id":1229627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229520-2e-how-much-space-between-demesne?p=1229621#post1229621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an Awareness Charm called Earth Reclaims Her Bounty. It transforms a DB into a Demesne of a level equal to her Breeding score.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> what book was that in? broken winged crane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T12:04:41-07:00","id":1229630,"title":"","content":"Ah, a Lords of Creation Charm.<br /> <br /> Well, if I would use that one in a game I'm running, I most likely would let it dry out after a while if used to close to an existing Demesne or Manse. Or perhaps dry out other ones if they were of a lower rating.<br /> <br /> Considering it requires an Essence 6+, Breeding 3+ Dragon Blood committing suicide to create a Demesne, I don't think there would be too many created that way anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, using the martyr effect inside an existing Demesne or Manse might have potential of some spectacular destructive effect (or doing nothing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T12:05:57-07:00","id":1229631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229520-2e-how-much-space-between-demesne?p=1229627#post1229627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what book was that in? broken winged crane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreams of the First Age: Lords of Creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T03:18:15-07:00","id":1231058,"title":"","content":"I use a formula as a rough guide.<br /> <br /> D = minimum distance between two demenses<br /> x = strongest demense level (assuming 4 for greater in EX3)<br /> y = weaker demense level (assuming 2 for lesser in EX3)<br /> z = matching type modifier : 1 for matching aspect, 2 for matching type (eg elemental, celestial), 3 for completely different<br /> <br /> D = (x+y)<sup>z</sup><br /> <br /> Which makes 2 level 5 manses of completely different type (for example, a fire and a lunar demense) have to be 125 miles apart, but 2 level 1 wood manses can be just 2 miles apart.<br /> <br /> This is for naturally occuring demenses, if the storyteller decides that the dragon lines have been altered by geomancy then an increase or decrease in demense density is reflected by the opposite effect somewhere relatively nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}